<title>GERMANY: VW, Opel lose market share during 1996 in Germany.</title>
<headline>VW, Opel lose market share during 1996 in Germany.</headline>
<dateline>FLENSBURG, Germany 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German federal motor office issued at the weekend the following information about German vehicle registrations for December and also for 1996. Information about Volkswagen includes sales of its foreign subsidiaries in Germany.</p>
<p>			     December   December</p>
<p>				 1996	 1995</p>
<p> Volkswagen		  39,650   41,653</p>
<p> Opel			  38,367   45,690</p>
<p> Ford			  24,607   22,088</p>
<p> BMW			   18,491   20,367</p>
<p> Audi			  15,981   13,015</p>
<p> Mercedes		    17,067   16,142</p>
<p> Seat			   4,439    4,318</p>
<p> Skoda			  1,418    1,673</p>
<p> Porsche	   251	280</p>
<p>		    Jan-Dec    Market     Jan-Dec  Market</p>
<p>		     1996	Share	1995	Share</p>
<p>Volkswagen	664,376    19.0 pct   643,739 19.4 pct</p>
<p>Opel		560,253    16.0 pct   553,188 16.7 pct</p>
<p>Ford		394,526    11.3 pct   376,179 11.4 pct</p>
<p>BMW		 227,321     6.5 pct   214,702 6.5 pct</p>
<p>Audi		214,537     6.1 pct   205,812 6.2 pct</p>
<p>Mercedes	  286,139     8.2 pct   250,334 7.6 pct</p>
<p>Seat		 53,214     1.5 pct    60,362 1.8 pct</p>
<p>Skoda		21,299     0.6 pct    20,595 0.6 pct</p>
<p>Porsche	     6,111     0.2 pct     5,895 0.2 pct</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
